{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaaYHwuM9P8ykcPHpmaa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I proved `myRep_add` in `Main.lean`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\n```lean\ntheorem myRep_add (a : α) (m n : Nat) : myRep a (m + n) = myRep a m ++ myRep a n := by\n  induction m with\n  | zero => simp [myRep]\n  | succ m ih => rw [Nat.succ_add, myRep, myRep, ih, List.cons_append]\n```\n\nThe proof works by induction on `m`:\n- **When `m` is 0:** `myRep a (0 + n)` simplifies to `[] ++ myRep a n`, and `simp` closes the goal.\n- **When `m` is `m + 1`:** `Nat.succ_add` rewrites `(m + 1) + n` as `(m + n) + 1`. Unfolding `myRep` on both sides then leaves `a :: myRep a (m + n) = (a :: myRep a m) ++ myRep a n`. The induction hypothesis and `List.cons_append` finish it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":477,"cache_read_input_tokens":7871,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":477},"output_tokens":346,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2b1e99c-0238-4a30-afa7-b049f6f353e0","uuid":"c69ee5f9-6304-4dd8-9bfe-1fc5ae45ea58","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:49:21.757Z","request_id":"req_011CgaaYHgmwDg2tmfDq15FZ"}
